From eb47ef5bb0cf08441e94eec24765754ce0ade80a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shyalya <shyalya@turtle-server.local>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 10:10:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Add world buffs, automatic donation points, and fix the
 donation shop
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

World buffs — each on its own independent timer, so they don't all fire at once:
- Spirit of Zandalar (24425): anyone in Stranglethorn Vale.
- Warchief's Blessing (16609): Horde only, in Crossroads or Orgrimmar (both locations share one timer, so they are always served simultaneously).
- Rallying Cry of the Dragonslayer (22888): both factions, each in their own capital — Alliance in Stormwind City, Horde in Orgrimmar (matches retail, where the Onyxia/Nefarian head is turned in at both capitals).
- The first roll after a (re)start uses a short interval (AutoWorldBuff.FirstMinInterval/FirstMaxInterval, default 10min-2h) so a server that restarts often doesn't delay the buffs by a full interval every time; later rolls use AutoWorldBuff.MinInterval/MaxInterval (default 1h-3h). A warning is announced AutoWorldBuff.WarningInterval (default 10min) beforehand.

AutoDonationPoints:
- Real online players (bots and the Discord bridge excluded) earn AutoDonationPoints.Amount donation points (shop_coins) per AutoDonationPoints.IntervalMs online, tracked per account so login time doesn't matter.
- Progress is persisted in the `donation_point_progress` table (login DB) and reloaded per account after a restart. It used to live in memory only and reset to zero on every restart, so with frequent restarts a normal player could never reach a full hour — while the permanently-connected Discord bridge was the only "session" that did. Written on every payout plus every AutoDonationPoints.FlushIntervalMs (default 5min).
- The bot/bridge exclusion now compares account names case-insensitively. It previously compared against "DISCORD" while the account is actually named "discord", so the Discord bridge itself collected the points and its chat output surfaced as "[Server]: You received ..." in the Discord channel.

Donation shop categories (bundled here because donation points are pointless without a working shop):
- The in-game "Donation Rewards" window showed only the "About" tab and no categories at all. The client's Shop_ProcessCategories (Interface\FrameXML\Turtle_ShopUI\Turtle_ShopUI.lua, inside patch-7.mpq) expects FOUR `=`-delimited fields per category — `id=parentId=name=icon` — and reads field 2 as the subcategory parent via tonumber(), then evaluates `if parentID > 0`. The server sent only three fields (`id=name=icon`), so field 2 was the category NAME, tonumber() returned nil, and comparing nil > 0 raised a Lua error that aborted the parse loop on the very first category.
- "About" still appeared because the client injects it itself as a synthetic `0=0=About=about;` entry (four fields, parses fine) before the server's first real category kills the loop — which is why the window looked half-alive rather than empty.
- This server has no subcategories (shop_categories has no parent column), so parentId is always sent as 0 = top-level. The sibling "Entries:" reply was already adapted to this client's 13-field format in ObjectMgr::LoadShop; only the category line had been missed.

Requires: new config keys (conf/) and the `donation_point_progress` table (sql/).
